Article 10. (1) Users conclude a sale contract with the Supplier as follows:
Register in the ONLINE STORE and provide the necessary details if not already registered, or order without registration;
Sign in to the ordering system using a username and password or another identification method;
Select one or more goods and add them to the purchase list;
Provide delivery details;
Choose the payment method and payment time;
Confirm the order.
(2) Users may also conclude a sale contract without registering, using the relevant online store interface functionality.

Article 14. (1) The Consumer may withdraw from the contract within 14 days of receiving the goods, without compensation or penalty and without giving a reason, using the standard withdrawal form on the Supplier’s website. Information about exercising this right is available on the website. Consumers may also use another unambiguous statement that can be recorded on a durable medium.
(2) This right does not apply to:
1. Goods made to the consumer’s order or individual specifications;
2. Goods liable to deteriorate or expire rapidly;
3. Sealed goods unsealed after delivery that cannot be returned for hygiene or health protection reasons;
4. Goods which, after delivery and by their nature, have become inseparably mixed with other goods;
5. Sealed audio or video recordings or sealed computer software unsealed after delivery;
6. Newspapers, periodicals or magazines, except subscription contracts for such publications.
(3) If the Supplier has not provided the information required under the Consumer Protection Act, the Consumer may withdraw within one year and 14 days from receipt of the goods. If the information is supplied within the withdrawal period, that period begins on the date it is supplied. The Consumer may notify the Supplier directly using the standard withdrawal form on the website.
(4) When the Consumer withdraws from a distance or off-premises contract, the Supplier reimburses all payments received, including delivery costs, without undue delay and no later than 14 days after being informed of the withdrawal decision. Reimbursement uses the same payment method as the initial transaction unless the Consumer expressly agrees otherwise and incurs no charges as a result.
(5) The Consumer bears the cost of returning the goods; return costs are deducted from the amount paid under the contract. The Supplier is not required to reimburse additional delivery costs where the Consumer expressly chose a method other than the least expensive standard delivery offered by the Supplier.
(6) The Consumer must keep the goods received and preserve their quality and safety during the period under paragraph 1.
(7) The Consumer may exercise withdrawal by sending a written statement using the standard form on the ONLINE STORE website.
(8) Unless the Supplier has offered to collect the goods itself, it may withhold reimbursement until it receives the goods or the Consumer supplies evidence of sending them back, whichever occurs first.

X. TERMINATION
Article 23. These General Terms and Conditions and the User’s contract with the Supplier terminate:
On dissolution and liquidation, or insolvency, of either contracting party;
By mutual written agreement;
Unilaterally, on notice by either party if the other fails to perform its obligations;
If either party is objectively unable to perform;
If state authorities seize or seal equipment;
If the User’s ONLINE STORE registration is deleted. Existing sale contracts not yet performed remain valid and must be performed;
If withdrawal is exercised under Article 55(1) of the Consumer Protection Act. In this case, only the contract for delivery of the particular ordered goods terminates, where withdrawal applies to that category of goods.
